    "https://recruiting2.ultipro.com/HER1009HRZ/JobBoard/267d2e37-abff-4559-8a18-a754503d3749/OpportunityDetail?opportunityId=8965da81-36df-4323-8a4a-631c3386022d": {
      "title": "Clinical Placement & Compliance Coordinator (Florida Region)",
      "description": "Clinical Placement & Compliance Coordinator (Florida Region). Current staff, faculty/adjunct at Herzing University: l og into UKG and navigate to Menu > Myself > ​My Company >​ View Opportunities to apply using the internal application process. The Clinical Placement & Compliance Coordinator (CPCC) supports the execution of clinical placement and compliance activities within an assigned region or program area. Reporting to the Director of Clinical Placement & Compliance, this position is responsible for coordinating student clinical placements, supporting student and faculty compliance requirements, maintaining accurate documentation, and providing operational support to ensure students are prepared and eligible to participate in clinical coursework. The coordinator serves as an operational liaison among students, faculty, clinical partners, and internal stakeholders to support timely placement, regulatory compliance, and positive clinical learning experiences. This role will support the Florida region. Schedule is primarily during standard business hours, with occasional evening and weekend responsibilities based on student and business needs. REQUIREMENTS: Bachelor’s degree required. 2 years’ experience required working in clinical, healthcare, office/auditing, or higher education setting. Prior experience in clinical coordination, healthcare administration, higher education operations, or related fields preferred. Familiarity with clinical education environments, regulatory requirements, or accreditation standards is preferred. Compensation is determined based on the qualifications, experience, and circumstances of each hire. It is uncommon for new employees to start near the top of the salary range. We offer a comprehensive benefits package, including a tuition waiver and reimbursement program, health insurance, paid time off, and a retirement savings plan with company match. The salary range for this role is $54,485 to $73,715. RESPONSIBILITIES: Student Clinical Placement Coordination: Coordinate student clinical placements in accordance with established timelines to ensure preparedness for clinical coursework. Maintain accurate placement records to ensure clinical experiences fulfill required hours, within the established timelines, and in accordance with university operating procedures. Evaluate clinical placement capacity and determine appropriate student assignments based on program and site requirements. Provide guidance and recommendations to students regarding clinical requirements, timelines, and progression, and exercising judgment to support successful outcomes. Prioritize competing placement issues based on program needs, risk, and stakeholder impact. Follow protocols established by affiliated clinical sites when requesting student placement and assigning students to clinical experiences. Assess clinical placement challenges and determine appropriate solutions, escalating only complex or high-risk issues to the Director of Clinical Placement & Compliance or appropriate leadership as needed. Clinical Compliance: Support student compliance processes to ensure all requirements are completed by established deadlines and prior to participation in clinical experiences. Track, verify, and maintain compliance documentation in accordance with university and clinical site requirements. Communicate compliance expectations, deadlines, and status updates to students and faculty in a timely manner. Assess student compliance issues and determine appropriate interventions or escalations in consultation with leadership. Analyze compliance data to identify potential risks, trends, or gaps and provide recommendations to leadership to improve processes or resolve issues. Communication & Stakeholder Coordination: Serve as a subject matter resource to students and faculty regarding clinical placement and compliance questions. Provide exceptional service to stakeholders through timely and professional communication to meet University expectations. Coordinate communication with clinical partners related to student rosters, schedules, and compliance documentation as directed. Collaborate with faculty, program leadership, and clinical teams to ensure alignment of placement and compliance activities. Document student status updates in accordance with operating procedures to ensure visibility and accuracy of on-going reporting. Participate in cross‑functional initiatives supporting clinical placement and compliance operations. All other duties as assigned. Click Here or use the following link to learn more about careers at Herzing University: https://tinyurl.com/HerzingU Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. We do not sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Must be able to remain in a stationary position most of the time. Must be able to occasionally move around the work location. Constantly operates office and/or teach equipment which may include computers, copiers, fax machines, audio/visuals. Frequently uses voice and hearing to communicate with students, staff, or colleagues face-to-face or over the telephone. Visually or otherwise identify, observe, and assess. Occasionally move, carry, or lift ten pounds. Herzing University is committed to providing a diverse environment and is dedicated to fostering a culture and atmosphere of mutual respect. It provides an inclusive and collegial community where individuals are valued, heard and empowered to contribute to the effectiveness of the institution. It is the university’s practice to recruit and hire without discrimination because of skin color, gender, religion, LGBTQi2+ status, disability status, age, national origin, veteran status, or any other status protected by law. https://www.herzing.edu/nondiscrimination-policy . Herzing University prohibits sex-based discrimination in any education program or activity that it operates. Individuals may report concerns or questions to the Title IX Coordinator. The notice of nondiscrimination is located at https://www.herzing.edu/title-ix ."
    },
    "https://recruiting2.ultipro.com/HER1009HRZ/JobBoard/267d2e37-abff-4559-8a18-a754503d3749/OpportunityDetail?opportunityId=9bac94d7-90ba-411e-9b20-6ff8e808a42e": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Graduate Business",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Graduate Business. If you are a current employee, faculty or adjunct instructor at Herzing University, log in to UKG > Menu > Myself > ​My Company >​ View Opportunities to apply using the internal application process. Herzing University's Atlanta Campus is looking for great individuals to fill adjunct faculty openings teaching Graduate level Business. Requirements: ​​Hold a doctorate in business or related area Have significant industry experience in related business field Have excellent communication and interpersonal skills Have the ability to engage and inspire students Compensation for this position is $900/per credit hour. The position's duties and responsibilities for this role include: Teaching and learning Scholarship of Teaching and Learning Academic and Institutional Service Within these duties and responsibilities, the following competencies are included. Subject Matter Expertise Effective Communication Pedagogical Mastery Operational Excellence Appreciation and Promotion of Diversity Assessment of Student Learning Utilization of Technology to Enhance Teaching and Learning Continuous Improvement These competencies, as identified by the University's academic community, encompass the knowledge, skills, and behaviors essential to a faculty member's success in the classroom and provide the basis for the faculty hiring, evaluation and development process. Click Here or use the following link to learn more about careers at Herzing University: https://tinyurl.com/HerzingU Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. We do not sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time. Herzing University is committed to providing a diverse environment and is dedicated to fostering a culture and atmosphere of mutual respect. It provides an inclusive and collegial community where individuals are valued, heard and empowered to contribute to the effectiveness of the institution. It is the university’s practice to recruit and hire without discrimination because of skin color, gender, religion, LGBTQi2+ status, disability status, age, national origin, veteran status, or any other status protected by law. https://www.herzing.edu/nondiscrimination-policy Herzing University prohibits sex-based discrimination in any education program or activity that it operates. Individuals may report concerns or questions to the Title IX Coordinator. The notice of nondiscrimination is located at https://www.herzing.edu/title-ix ."
    },
    "https://recruiting2.ultipro.com/HER1009HRZ/JobBoard/267d2e37-abff-4559-8a18-a754503d3749/OpportunityDetail?opportunityId=39e3fb1c-d96a-4cda-be0f-5005493c144e": {
      "title": "Program Chair - Radiologic Technology",
      "description": "Program Chair - Radiologic Technology. Current staff, faculty/adjunct at Herzing University, log into UKG and navigate to Menu > Myself > ​My Company > ​ View Opportunities to apply using the internal application process. This role will be onsite at the Atlanta, GA campus. Requirements: Associate's Degree in Radiologic Technology Bachelor's (in any field) required, Masters or willing to obtain Masters preferred) ARRT (R) Certification Teaching and clinical experience is required At least 2 years of supervisory experience preferred Compensation is determined based on the qualifications, experience, and circumstances of each hire. It is uncommon for new employees to start near the top of the salary range. We offer a comprehensive benefits package, including a tuition waiver and reimbursement program, health insurance, paid time off, and a retirement savings plan. The salary range for this position is $88,434 to $119,646. The Program Chair engages with candidates for enrollment and with students. This position actively participates in new student orientation, contributes to various committees, and contributes to faculty and staff training. As an academic leader, the Program Chair plays a visible role for our students as well. This can include provision of student advising, resolution of student complaints, and/or intervention when student engagement or academic progress is in question. The following competencies, as identified by the University’s academic community, encompass the knowledge, skills, and behaviors essential to a Program Chair’s success. These will also provide the basis for Program Chair hiring, evaluation and professional development. Engagement in the Curriculum Development Process Communication Support of Pedagogical Mastery Operational Excellence Utilization of Technology to Enhance Teaching, Learning, and Program Development Promotion and Maintenance of a Positive Learning Environment and Department Culture Continuous Improvement Instructional Practice Management/Supervision Click Here or use the following link to learn more about careers at Herzing University: https://tinyurl.com/HerzingU Herzing University is committed to providing a diverse environment and is dedicated to fostering a culture and atmosphere of mutual respect. It provides an inclusive and collegial community where individuals are valued, heard and empowered to contribute to the effectiveness of the institution. Physical requirements: Must be able to remain in a stationary position most of the time. Must be able to occasionally move around the work location. Must be able to communicate information and ideas so others will understand. Constantly operates office and/or tech equipment which may include computers, copiers, fax machines, audio/visuals. Frequently uses voice and hearing to communicate with students, staff or colleagues face-to-face or over the telephone. Visually or otherwise identify, observe and assess. Occasionally move, carry, or lift 10 pounds. Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. We do not sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time. It is the university’s practice to recruit and hire without discrimination because of skin color, gender, religion, LGBTQi2+ status, disability status, age, national origin, veteran status, or any other status protected by law. https://www.herzing.edu/nondiscrimination-policy Herzing University prohibits sex-based discrimination in any education program or activity that it operates. Individuals may report concerns or questions to the Title IX Coordinator. The notice of nondiscrimination is located at https://www.herzing.edu/title-ix"
    },
    "https://recruiting2.ultipro.com/HER1009HRZ/JobBoard/267d2e37-abff-4559-8a18-a754503d3749/OpportunityDetail?opportunityId=cbdbe2ff-00cc-4332-8c36-2e0f27b27ff6": {
      "title": "Senior Financial Aid Advisor - Team Lead",
      "description": "Senior Financial Aid Advisor - Team Lead. Current staff, faculty/adjunct at Herzing University: log into UKG and navigate to Menu > Myself > ​My Company > ​ View Opportunities to apply using the internal application process. This role supports Herzing University's Midwest Region and will be located onsite at one of the Midwest Campuses - Akron, OH; Brookfield, WI; Kenosha, WI; Madison, WI; Minneapolis, MN. The Senior Financial Aid Advisor – Team Lead supports Herzing University’s mission through administration of financial aid funding for the University’s students. This role requires strong customer service and attention to detail. This individual may work directly with students, providing counseling and assistance on all aspects of the financial aid process, or the individual may work to package, process, and award financial aid funds. Additionally, this individual assists their supervisor with management responsibilities for their team or region. A 40-hour schedule will be determined based on business needs Monday through Friday with a start as early as 8am with one late night scheduled until 7pm. REQUIREMENTS: Bachelor’s degree preferred. Minimum of one-year Senior level Financial Aid or related work experience required. 3-5 years of Title IV administration experience preferred. Compensation is determined based on the qualifications, experience, and circumstances of each hire. It is uncommon for new employees to start near the top of the salary range. We offer a comprehensive benefits package, including a tuition waiver and reimbursement program, health insurance, paid time off, and a retirement savings plan. The hourly pay range for this position is $26.35 to $35.65. RESPONSIBILITIES: Meet with new students to understand funding needs, provide guidance on completion of the FAFSA and required documents, and review eligibility for funding options including Federal Title IV funds, scholarships, state funding, and military funds. Utilize financial aid software to review student documents and eligibility criteria to finalize financial aid awards. Provide gap funding options to students and support students in determining the best option to meet their financial needs and support their educational goals. Counsel students on financial literacy and wellness topics for the purpose of educating and encouraging responsible borrowing practices. Manage a student caseload, striving to build relationships and support students in resolving all matters related to their financial aid funding. Perform regular outreach to students requiring action including needed documents, loan acceptance, and past due balances. Revise financial aid award packages due to updates such as changes in course schedules, approved breaks, eligibility changes, and other factors. Troubleshoot disbursement rejects and resolve factors preventing timely disbursement of funding. Provide an average of 5 hours per week assisting with management responsibilities for the team or region. Examples may include, but are not limited to, management of Federal Work Study staff, managing team processes, responding to staff questions, leading projects, and assisting with onboarding new team members. Dedication to continuous improvement especially in the areas of student satisfaction and accuracy. Demonstrate all aspects of the PRICE of Success. Herzing University is committed to providing a diverse environment and is dedicated to fostering a culture and atmosphere of mutual respect. It provides an inclusive and collegial community where individuals are valued, heard and empowered to contribute to the effectiveness of the institution. Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. We do not sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Must be able to remain in a stationary position most of the time. Must be able to occasionally move around the work location. Constantly operates office and/or teach equipment which may include computers, copiers, fax machines, audio/visuals. Frequently uses voice and hearing to communicate with students, staff or colleagues face-to-face or over the telephone. Visually or otherwise identify, observe and assess. Occasionally move, carry, or lift 10 pounds. Click Here or use the following link to learn more about careers at Herzing University: https://tinyurl.com/HerzingU It is the university’s practice to recruit and hire without discrimination because of skin color, gender, religion, LGBTQi2+ status, disability status, age, national origin, veteran status, or any other status protected by law. https://www.herzing.edu/about/diversity Herzing University prohibits sex-based discrimination in any education program or activity that it operates. Individuals may report concerns or questions to the Title IX Coordinator. The notice of nondiscrimination is located at https://www.herzing.edu/title-ix ."
