    "https://recruiting2.ultipro.com/HER1009HRZ/JobBoard/267d2e37-abff-4559-8a18-a754503d3749/OpportunityDetail?opportunityId=68f01b6d-541a-4dda-9b35-c6c6ce70e02d": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty -  Doctorate of Behavioral Health (Online Division)",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Doctorate of Behavioral Health (Online Division). Current staff, faculty/adjunct at Herzing University: l og into UKG and navigate to Menu > Myself > ​My Company >​ View Opportunities to apply using the internal application process. Adjunct Faculty are eligible to participate in the Herzing 401(k) plan with a generous company match and our excellent education assistance programs! Click Here or use the following link to learn more about careers at Herzing University: https://tinyurl.com/HerzingU The primary responsibility of Adjunct Faculty is to create a learning environment that is engaging, inspiring, and supports students in achieving their highest academic potential. Requirements: Doctor of Behavioral Health (DBH) degree required 2 years of practice experience post DBH degree Online teaching experience preferred Specialized Subjects areas for teaching: Research, Data Analytics, Neuropsychology, Pharmacology; other subject areas also considered Compensation for this role is $900 per credit hour. The job of faculty members at Herzing University has three dimensions: Teaching and learning Scholarship of Teaching and Learning Academic and Institutional Service Within the above duties and responsibilities, the following competencies are included. Subject Matter Expertise Effective Communication Pedagogical Mastery Operational Excellence Appreciation and Promotion of Diversity Assessment of Student Learning Utilization of Technology to Enhance Teaching and Learning Continuous Improvement These competencies, as identified by the University's academic community, encompass the knowledge, skills, and behaviors essential to a faculty member's success in the classroom and provide the basis for the faculty hiring, evaluation and development process. Herzing University is committed to providing a diverse environment and is dedicated to fostering a culture and atmosphere of mutual respect. It provides an inclusive and collegial community where individuals are valued, heard and empowered to contribute to the effectiveness of the institution. Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. We do not sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time. It is the university’s practice to recruit and hire without discrimination because of skin color, gender, religion, LGBTQi2+ status, disability status, age, national origin, veteran status, or any other status protected by law. https://www.herzing.edu/nondiscrimination-policy Herzing University prohibits sex-based discrimination in any education program or activity that it operates. Individuals may report concerns or questions to the Title IX Coordinator. The notice of nondiscrimination is located at https://www.herzing.edu/title-ix ."
    },
    "https://recruiting2.ultipro.com/HER1009HRZ/JobBoard/267d2e37-abff-4559-8a18-a754503d3749/OpportunityDetail?opportunityId=d6572e62-f1c6-435e-a8d3-5357c80cf1a3": {
      "title": "Clinical Placement & Compliance Coordinator",
      "description": "Clinical Placement & Compliance Coordinator. Current staff, faculty/adjunct at Herzing University: l og into UKG and navigate to Menu > Myself > ​My Company >​ View Opportunities to apply using the internal application process. The Clinical Placement & Compliance Coordinator (CPCC) supports the execution of clinical placement and compliance activities within an assigned region or program area. Reporting to the Director of Clinical Placement & Compliance, this position is responsible for coordinating student clinical placements, supporting student and faculty compliance requirements, maintaining accurate documentation, and providing operational support to ensure students are prepared and eligible to participate in clinical coursework. The coordinator serves as an operational liaison among students, faculty, clinical partners, and internal stakeholders to support timely placement, regulatory compliance, and positive clinical learning experiences. The position is based onsite at the Atlanta (Sandy Springs) campus and supports both campus-based and online programs, with the potential for a hybrid work schedule. REQUIREMENTS: Bachelor’s degree required. 2 years’ experience required working in clinical, healthcare, office/auditing, or higher education setting. Prior experience in clinical coordination, healthcare administration, higher education operations, or related fields preferred. Familiarity with clinical education environments, regulatory requirements, or accreditation standards is preferred. Compensation is determined based on the qualifications, experience, and circumstances of each hire. It is uncommon for new employees to start near the top of the salary range. We offer a comprehensive benefits package, including a tuition waiver and reimbursement program, health insurance, paid time off, and a retirement savings plan with company match. The salary range for this role is $54,485 to $73,715. Click Here or use the following link to learn more about careers at Herzing University: https://tinyurl.com/HerzingU RESPONSIBILITIES: Student Clinical Placement Coordination: Coordinate student clinical placements in accordance with established timelines to ensure preparedness for clinical coursework. Maintain accurate placement records to ensure clinical experiences fulfill required hours, within the established timelines, and in accordance with university operating procedures. Evaluate clinical placement capacity and determine appropriate student assignments based on program and site requirements. Provide guidance and recommendations to students regarding clinical requirements, timelines, and progression, and exercising judgment to support successful outcomes. Prioritize competing placement issues based on program needs, risk, and stakeholder impact. Follow protocols established by affiliated clinical sites when requesting student placement and assigning students to clinical experiences. Assess clinical placement challenges and determine appropriate solutions, escalating only complex or high-risk issues to the Director of Clinical Placement & Compliance or appropriate leadership as needed. Clinical Compliance: Support student compliance processes to ensure all requirements are completed by established deadlines and prior to participation in clinical experiences. Track, verify, and maintain compliance documentation in accordance with university and clinical site requirements. Communicate compliance expectations, deadlines, and status updates to students and faculty in a timely manner. Assess student compliance issues and determine appropriate interventions or escalations in consultation with leadership. Analyze compliance data to identify potential risks, trends, or gaps and provide recommendations to leadership to improve processes or resolve issues. Communication & Stakeholder Coordination: Serve as a subject matter resource to students and faculty regarding clinical placement and compliance questions. Provide exceptional service to stakeholders through timely and professional communication to meet University expectations. Coordinate communication with clinical partners related to student rosters, schedules, and compliance documentation as directed. Collaborate with faculty, program leadership, and clinical teams to ensure alignment of placement and compliance activities. Document student status updates in accordance with operating procedures to ensure visibility and accuracy of on-going reporting. Participate in cross‑functional initiatives supporting clinical placement and compliance operations. All other duties as assigned. Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. We do not sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Must be able to remain in a stationary position most of the time. Must be able to occasionally move around the work location. Constantly operates office and/or teach equipment which may include computers, copiers, fax machines, audio/visuals. Frequently uses voice and hearing to communicate with students, staff, or colleagues face-to-face or over the telephone. Visually or otherwise identify, observe, and assess. Occasionally move, carry, or lift ten pounds. Herzing University is committed to providing a diverse environment and is dedicated to fostering a culture and atmosphere of mutual respect. It provides an inclusive and collegial community where individuals are valued, heard and empowered to contribute to the effectiveness of the institution. It is the university’s practice to recruit and hire without discrimination because of skin color, gender, religion, LGBTQi2+ status, disability status, age, national origin, veteran status, or any other status protected by law. https://www.herzing.edu/nondiscrimination-policy Herzing University prohibits sex-based discrimination in any education program or activity that it operates. Individuals may report concerns or questions to the Title IX Coordinator. The notice of nondiscrimination is located at https://www.herzing.edu/title-ix ."
    },
    "https://recruiting2.ultipro.com/HER1009HRZ/JobBoard/267d2e37-abff-4559-8a18-a754503d3749/OpportunityDetail?opportunityId=7d25c652-bcbb-4859-9403-3c73cbb87cfd": {
      "title": "Human Resources Generalist (Temporary)",
      "description": "Human Resources Generalist (Temporary). Current staff, faculty/adjunct at Herzing University: log into UKG and navigate to Menu > Myself > ​My Company >​ View Opportunities to apply using the internal application process. This is a temporary position (approx. 3-6 months) supporting critical HR operational and compliance functions during a high-volume period. Herzing University is seeking a detail-oriented and service-oriented HR Operations & Employee Services Coordinator to temporarily support critical HR operations and employee lifecycle activities. This role is primarily responsible for administering the University's Form I-9 and employment eligibility verification program, supporting employee onboarding, managing employment verification requests, and serving as a key resource for employee and manager inquiries. This position requires an individual with prior experience managing high-volume I-9 processing and onboarding activities while maintaining exceptional accuracy, compliance, and customer service. The successful candidate will be highly organized, adaptable, and comfortable working in a fast-paced environment with competing priorities and deadlines. This role may also provide broader operational and administrative support to the HR department based on business needs and workload capacity. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Minimum of two years of Human Resources, Employee Services, HR Operations, or related experience. Demonstrated experience administering Form I-9 employment eligibility verification, including high-volume processing and compliance management. Experience supporting high-volume hiring, onboarding, or employee lifecycle transactions with a strong focus on accuracy and compliance. Strong understanding of employee records management and confidentiality requirements. Exceptional organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities, deadlines, and competing demands. Strong attention to detail and commitment to accuracy. Excellent customer service, communication, and problem-solving skills. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications and HR systems. Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively with a remote team. Preferred Qualifications: Experience serving as an I-9 Administrator or supporting an organization-wide I-9 program. Experience training others on I-9 compliance and employment verification procedures. Experience supporting a multi-location or multi-state workforce. Experience with HRIS systems such as UKG. Experience in higher education or a similarly complex organization. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES: HR Compliance & I-9 Program Administration Serve as the primary administrator of the Form I-9 and employment eligibility verification program, ensuring compliance with federal requirements. Coordinate and complete high-volume employment eligibility verifications for new hires across multiple locations and employee populations. Provide training, guidance, and support to designated I-9 Administrators to ensure consistency and compliance across the organization. Monitor processes, identify opportunities for improvement, and maintain documentation related to employment eligibility verification. Assist with I-9 audits, compliance reviews, and corrective action efforts when necessary. Employment Verification & HR Records Administration Manage and respond to employment verification requests, including Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) certifications and other employment-related documentation. Ensure timely, accurate, and confidential handling of employee records and sensitive information. Maintain HR documentation and support audit readiness initiatives. Assist with record maintenance and documentation requirements throughout the employee lifecycle. Employee & Manager Support Serve as the primary point of contact for the HR phone line, providing professional and responsive customer service. Manage the HR shared inbox by responding to inquiries, resolving requests when appropriate, and routing matters to the appropriate HR team members. Provide support and guidance regarding HR processes and procedures to employees and managers. Onboarding & New Hire Administration Support onboarding activities, including employment eligibility verification, employee photo management, login assistance, and general new hire support. Cross-train on new hire processing activities and provide operational support during periods of high hiring volume. Assist in ensuring a positive onboarding experience through timely communication and issue resolution. Administrative & Operational Support Manage incoming HR mail, including receipt, scanning, electronic filing, and routing of documents to a remote HR team. Provide administrative support to HR operational processes and projects as needed. Assist with maintaining HR documentation, records, forms, job descriptions, organizational charts, and other departmental resources. Support employee recognition and service milestone programs, including anniversary gift coordination and tracking. Assist with audits, process improvement initiatives, special projects, and other HR operational priorities as assigned. THE COMPENSATION range for this temporary role is $22.00 to $29.00 per hour. THE IDEAL CANDIDATE IS: Highly organized and detail-oriented. Experienced in managing high-volume HR transactions. Comfortable working independently and taking ownership of assigned responsibilities. Service-oriented with a strong commitment to employee and manager support. Adaptable and able to shift priorities as business needs change. Committed to compliance, accuracy, and continuous process improvement. Click Here or use the following link to learn more about careers at Herzing University: https://tinyurl.com/HerzingU Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. We do not sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time. Herzing University is committed to providing a diverse environment and is dedicated to fostering a culture and atmosphere of mutual respect. It provides an inclusive and collegial community where individuals are valued, heard and empowered to contribute to the effectiveness of the institution. It is the university’s practice to recruit and hire without discrimination because of skin color, gender, religion, LGBTQi2+ status, disability status, age, national origin, veteran status, or any other status protected by law. https://www.herzing.edu/nondiscrimination-policy Herzing University prohibits sex-based discrimination in any education program or activity that it operates. Individuals may report concerns or questions to the Title IX Coordinator. The notice of nondiscrimination is located at https://www.herzing.edu/title-ix ."
    },
    "https://recruiting2.ultipro.com/HER1009HRZ/JobBoard/267d2e37-abff-4559-8a18-a754503d3749/OpportunityDetail?opportunityId=9e03be31-4f41-4f31-a3fe-96a65cdf0fae": {
      "title": "Faculty Clinical Coordinator - Surgical Technology",
      "description": "Faculty Clinical Coordinator - Surgical Technology. Current staff, faculty/adjunct at Herzing University: log into UKG and navigate to Menu > Myself > ​My Company > ​ View Opportunities to apply using the internal application process. The Faculty Clinical Coordinator for Surgical Technology will ensure that a minimum of one clinical preceptor must be designated at each recognized clinical setting. Ensure all assigned preceptors meet the credentialing requirements of assigned facilities and that all required documentation is maintained according to Herzing University Policy. The coordinator implements and teaches an orientation program for all clinical preceptors to ensure that program outcomes are being met. The coordinator documents that the site is meeting accreditation standards at least once per clinical rotation through a site visit or other communication means. Courses taught will be clinical and labs. Requirements: Associate's degree in related discipline, Bachelor's degree preferred. ​ Be a graduate of an education program in surgical technology accredited by a nationally recognized programmatic accreditation agency Posses a credential in the field of surgical technology through a national certification program that is accredited by the National Commission on Certifying Agencies (NCAA) Have at least 3 years of experience in the operating room scrub role or as an instructor in surgical technology (or a combination of both) within the past 5 years. Strong interpersonal and relationship-building skills necessary to maintain positive, professional interactions with students, alumni, faculty, and employer partners. Experience teaching hands on skills to new surgical technologists or students. Excellent presentation and communication skills, with the ability to convey ideas effectively to individuals and groups. Preferred that candidate demonstrates knowledge of programmatic accreditation and regulatory standards established by CAAHEP for Surgical Technology programs Compensation is determined based on the qualifications, experience, and circumstances of each hire. It is uncommon for new employees to start near the top of the salary range. We offer a comprehensive benefits package, including a tuition waiver and reimbursement program, health insurance, paid time off, and a retirement savings plan with company match. The salary range for this position is $60,690 to $82,110. Clinical Coordination Duties: Maintain an up-to-date knowledge of the profession to include trends in practice and education, compliance with governing body’s policies and procedures, competitive and collaborative practices with regards to other programs in the area, and any other information regarding practice that might impact the achievement of program outcomes. Identify, select, contract with, monitor, and evaluate all clinical sites. Maintain site selection criteria and contract documentation in support of competency requirements. Visit all clinical sites at least once each rotation to ensure sites continue to support a relevant and comprehensive experience as appropriate. Work in conjunction with the program administrator to establish clinical schedules and evaluate student clinical learning experiences. Work in conjunction with the internship/practicum course coordinator to place students for their internship/practicum assignment. Advise the program administrator on program areas of interest, i.e. industry trends; program statistics, analysis, and recommendations; clinical site availability, opportunities, and appropriateness; student performance; areas of concern, etc. Provide recommendations and address concerns to the program administrator on the competency and clinical management skills of clinical faculty, as well as compliance with clinical facility policies and procedures. Participate in the program planning process. Comply with all policies and procedures and make recommendations for changes when appropriate. Establish and maintain a system to ensure the timely and accurate completion and submission of facility, campus, system, government and accrediting agency reports related to the clinical experience. Participate in Partner relations including, but not limited to, active participation in related professional associations, and building business connections in the community. Ensure all necessary facility-required documentation and training is completed in a timely and appropriate manner. Provide orientation, training, and development guidance to faculty and students regarding their clinical site. Assist the program administrator with the evaluation and training of clinical instructors. Provide recommendations to the program administrator concerning the upkeep and purchase of subject-specific hardware, software and other media Serve as the first point of contact for resolution of clinical personnel issues, which may arise between staff at the clinical site and clinical faculty and students. Engages program administrator as appropriate in facilitating the resolution of clinical personnel issues if further intervention is needed. Participate in course meetings arranged by the course leads to ensure that clinical settings are meeting the needs of the course. Support and constructively contribute to campus decision-making processes. Provide advisement support regarding clinical expectations and performance to students. Participate in professional development activities, professional organizations, and partnership activities. Accept and complete additional related duties as assigned by the program administrator. Work in conjunction with the program administrator to establish clinical schedules and evaluate student clinical learning experiences. Work in conjunction with the program administrator to place students for their practicum, assignment The position's duties and responsibilities for this role include: Teaching and learning Scholarship of Teaching and Learning Academic and Institutional Service Within these duties and responsibilities, the following competencies are included. Subject Matter Expertise Effective Communication Pedagogical Mastery Operational Excellence Appreciation and Promotion of Diversity Assessment of Student Learning Utilization of Technology to Enhance Teaching and Learning Continuous Improvement Herzing University is committed to providing a diverse environment and is dedicated to fostering a culture and atmosphere of mutual respect. It provides an inclusive and collegial community where individuals are valued, heard and empowered to contribute to the effectiveness of the institution. Click Here or use the following link to learn more about careers at Herzing University: https://tinyurl.com/HerzingU Physical Requirements: Must be able to remain in a stationary position 50% of the time. Ability to move about readily and rapidly, if necessary, around campus, classrooms, clinical settings, etc., to access classrooms, desks, students, office machinery, clinics, patients, etc. Constantly communicates using the spoken word with students, staff and colleagues. Visually or otherwise identify, observe and assess. Operate equipment specific to programmatic track, personal computer, audio-visual equipment, clinical equipment, etc. Travel to off-site meetings or conferences or to observe students during clinical education at off-site clinical settings. In addition to the above requirements, for programs that include a clinical component, all faculty must be able to: Stand and/or walk for extended periods of time. Ability to reach by extending hands or arms in any direction. Finger dexterity required to manipulate objects. Ability to see and hear within normal parameters. Lift up to 25 pounds. Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. We do not sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time. It is the university’s practice to recruit and hire without discrimination because of skin color, gender, religion, LGBTQi2+ status, disability status, age, national origin, veteran status, or any other status protected by law. https://www.herzing.edu/nondiscrimination-policy Herzing University prohibits sex-based discrimination in any education program or activity that it operates. Individuals may report concerns or questions to the Title IX Coordinator. The notice of nondiscrimination is located at https://www.herzing.edu/title-ix ."
