      "title": "Program Chair - Mathematics (Online Division)",
      "description": "Program Chair - Mathematics (Online Division). To participate in a remote work arrangement, employees must reside in the United States. No remote work arrangement will be considered for working from outside the United States. Current staff, faculty/adjunct at Herzing University: log into UKG and navigate to Menu > Myself > ​My Company >​ View Opportunities to apply using the internal application process. Requirements A Master's degree in Mathematics or Statistics At least five years of higher education experience Management experience highly preferred Compensation is determined based on the qualifications, experience, and circumstances of each hire. It is uncommon for new employees to start near the top of the salary range. We offer a comprehensive benefits package, including a tuition waiver and reimbursement program, health insurance, paid time off, and a retirement savings plan with company match. The salary range for this position is $61,501 to $83,207. Summary of Primary Responsibilities As a member of the academic leadership team, your responsibilities include hiring, training, developing and evaluating staff and faculty, and supervision of both faculty and staff, but extends to programmatic management as well. This may include data collection, analysis and reporting, and continuous improvement. Experience with programmatic accreditation is desired. Duties and responsibilities for this role include: Teaching and learning Scholarship of Teaching and Learning Academic and Institutional Service Within these duties and responsibilities, the following competencies are included. Subject Matter Expertise Effective Communication Pedagogical Mastery Operational Excellence Appreciation and Promotion of Diversity Assessment of Student Learning Utilization of Technology to Enhance Teaching and Learning The above competencies, as identified by the University’s academic community, encompass the knowledge, skills, and behaviors essential to a Program Chair’s success. These will also provide the basis for Program Chair hiring, evaluation and professional development. Click Here or use the following link to learn more about careers at Herzing University: https://tinyurl.com/HerzingU Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. We do not sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time. Physical Requirements: Must be able to remain in a stationary position most of the time. Must be able to occasionally move around the work location. Must be able to communicate information and ideas so others will understand. Constantly operates office and/or tech equipment which may include computers, copiers, fax machines, audio/visuals. Frequently uses voice and hearing to communicate with students, staff or colleagues face-to-face or over the telephone. Visually or otherwise identify, observe and assess. Occasionally move, carry, or lift 10 pounds. It is the university’s practice to recruit and hire without discrimination because of skin color, gender, religion, LGBTQi2+ status, disability status, age, national origin, veteran status, or any other status protected by law. https://www.herzing.edu/nondiscrimination-policy Herzing University prohibits sex-based discrimination in any education program or activity that it operates. Individuals may report concerns or questions to the Title IX Coordinator. The notice of nondiscrimination is located at https://www.herzing.edu/title-ix ."
    },
    "https://recruiting2.ultipro.com/HER1009HRZ/JobBoard/267d2e37-abff-4559-8a18-a754503d3749/OpportunityDetail?opportunityId=e1e0c8d1-62d5-4aa6-aa78-531320be3c61": {
      "title": "Director of IT, Business Analysis & Project Management",
      "description": "Director of IT, Business Analysis & Project Management. Current staff, faculty/adjunct at Herzing University: log into UKG and navigate to Menu > Myself > ​My Company >​ View Opportunities to apply using the internal application process. To participate in a remote work arrangement, employees must reside in the United States. No remote work arrangement will be considered for working from outside the United States. Overview: The Director of IT, Business Analysis & Project Management, will lead the Business Analysis and Project Management practices and execution of the demand management process. This role is accountable for maturing disciplined project delivery, aligning technology demand to institutional priorities, and ensuring consistent, effective execution across the portfolio. This position reports to Vice President of Strategic Execution and manages Business Analysts, Project Managers, and related project resources. The role partners closely with IT leadership, functional leaders, Business Intelligence, and vendor partners to support portfolio planning, project execution, reporting, adoption, and continuous improvement. REQUIREMENTS: Bachelor’s degree in information technology, Business, Project Management, or a related field. 10+ years of experience in project management, business analysis, practice leadership. 5+ years of people leadership experience managing project managers, business analysts, or similar professional staff. Strong experience with demand management, project lifecycle management, portfolio planning, executive reporting, and stakeholder engagement. Demonstrated experience leading cross-functional initiatives, facilitating prioritization discussions, and communicating effectively with senior leaders. Proven ability to improve processes, define operating routines, establish metrics, and drive accountability across teams. Experience working in governed environments with attention to risk, compliance, stakeholder communication, and documentation discipline. Experience partnering with vendors, systems integrators, business stakeholders, and technical teams to deliver project outcomes. Preferred Qualifications: PMP, PMI-PBA, CBAP, Agile, or related certification. Master's degree in a related field. Higher education experience or experience in a complex, matrixed organization. Experience with Salesforce CRM, Agentforce Education, enterprise systems, portfolio management tools, Power BI, or similar reporting platforms. Experience supporting AI, data, digital transformation, or enterprise modernization initiatives. Compensation is determined based on the qualifications, experience, and circumstances of each hire. It is uncommon for new employees to start near the top of the salary range. We offer a comprehensive benefits package, including a tuition waiver and reimbursement program, health insurance, paid time off, and a retirement savings plan. The salary range for this position is $124,270 to $168,130. RESPONSIBILITIES: Project Management Leadership Define, mature, and scale IT project management and business analysis standards, including lifecycle checkpoints, templates, reporting routines, and execution expectations across the portfolio. Provide direct leadership, coaching, prioritization guidance, and performance management for Business Analysts, Project Managers, and related project resources. Partner closely with IT Directors, Solutions Architect, and technical delivery leads to align schedules, balance capacity constraints, remove execution blockers, and ensure smooth handoffs from requirements to implementation. Ensure initiatives follow the IT project lifecycle, approval gates, and escalation processes, applying enhanced oversight for large, complex, key priorities or strategic initiatives, including milestone reviews, executive visibility, readiness reviews, and go/no-go checkpoints. Oversee project scope, schedules, dependencies, risks, resource constraints, and change readiness to keep initiatives on track and aligned with institutional objectives. Establish portfolio management practices that balance strategic priorities, resource capacity, and risk, while tracking portfolio level metrics such as on time delivery, stakeholder satisfaction, process compliance, and ROI realization. Business Analysis Practice Leadership Lead the Business Analysis practice and define standards for requirements management, process analysis, stakeholder engagement, documentation, and solution evaluation. Mentor and develop Business Analysts to improve consistency, quality, business partnership, and consultative capabilities. Ensure business needs, acceptance criteria, desired outcomes, and operational impacts are clearly defined before significant IT effort is committed. Partner with stakeholders and delivery teams to shape requests, clarify scope, and improve quality of demand entering the project pipeline. Drive continuous improvement of Business Analysis methods, templates, quality reviews, and integration with project delivery processes. Demand Management & Prioritization Execute and coordinate the IT demand management process from requirements gathering through scheduling and completion, partnering with IT governance leadership on prioritization, approvals, and ROI realization. Lead Business Analysts in evaluating incoming requests against strategic alignment, resource needs, risk, complexity, and readiness to ensure rigorous intake execution. Participate in stakeholder discussions with IT leadership and functional stakeholders to align demand with capacity, roadmap commitments, and institutional priorities. Collaborate with IT governance leadership in maintaining accurate demand and portfolio data to support roadmap planning, capacity management, and leadership reporting. Leadership, Cross-Functional Influence & Adoption Partner with AI leadership to translate institutional strategy and business needs identified through the BA practice into well-defined requirements that inform AI use case prioritization and delivery. Support AI leadership in driving change management, operational integration, and user enablement to accelerate adoption of deployed AI and digital transformation solutions. Engage senior IT and university business leaders to facilitate prioritization discussions, align cross-departmental expectations, and sustain change readiness across the portfolio. Champion responsible for AI use, data security, and ethical practice standards across the BA and PM practice, consistent with Herzing's AI Governance standards, in coordination with AI leadership on enterprise AI initiatives. Executive Reporting & Operational Management Develop executive-ready dashboards, portfolio summaries, project health views, and action-oriented leadership reporting. Provide visibility into demand pipeline, project status, resource utilization, risks, delivery performance, and ROI realization. Lead recurring portfolio reviews and operating routines with clear decisions, next steps, and owners. Support annual roadmap development, investment prioritization, strategic planning, and operational execution planning. Identify operational bottlenecks and recommend improvements to increase throughput, predictability, transparency, and stakeholder confidence. Click Here or use the following link to learn more about careers at Herzing University: https://tinyurl.com/HerzingU Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. We do not sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Must be able to remain in a stationary position most of the time. Must be able to occasionally move around the work location. Constantly operates office and/or tech equipment which may include computers, copiers, fax machines, audio/visuals. Frequently uses voice and hearing to communicate with students, staff or colleagues face-to-face or over the telephone. Visually or otherwise identify, observe and assess. Occasionally move, carry, or lift 10 pounds. Frequently positions self to maintain computer related equipment which may involve bending, stooping, kneeling, crouching, or crawling. Herzing University is committed to providing a diverse environment and is dedicated to fostering a culture and atmosphere of mutual respect. It provides an inclusive and collegial community where individuals are valued, heard and empowered to contribute to the effectiveness of the institution. It is the university’s practice to recruit and hire without discrimination because of skin color, gender, religion, LGBTQi2+ status, disability status, age, national origin, veteran status, or any other status protected by law. https://www.herzing.edu/nondiscrimination-policy Herzing University prohibits sex-based discrimination in any education program or activity that it operates. Individuals may report concerns or questions to the Title IX Coordinator. The notice of nondiscrimination is located at https://www.herzing.edu/title-ix ."
    },
    "https://recruiting2.ultipro.com/HER1009HRZ/JobBoard/267d2e37-abff-4559-8a18-a754503d3749/OpportunityDetail?opportunityId=1fde6545-b5cc-4bab-a343-1adaaff1c54a": {
      "title": "Director of Curriculum - Prelicensure Nursing",
      "description": "Director of Curriculum - Prelicensure Nursing. Current staff, faculty/adjunct at Herzing University: log into UKG and navigate to Menu > Myself > ​My Company >​ View Opportunities to apply using the internal application process. To participate in a remote work arrangement, employees must reside in the United States. No remote work arrangement will be considered for working from outside the United States. Overview: the Director of Curriculum leads the design, development, review, implementation, and continuous improvement of nursing curriculum across all Herzing University prelicensure nursing programs. The Director ensures that curriculum is academically rigorous, aligned with accreditation standards, reflective of current nursing practice and evidence, and consistently implemented across all delivery modalities. The Director of Curriculum provides direct supervision to assigned personnel, to support faculty driven curriculum and assessment at Herzing University. The Director coordinates curriculum strategy, ensures consistent implementation across programs, and maintains a consistent and continuous communication strategy with all stakeholders to advance faculty ownership of prelicensure nursing curriculum and assessment. REQUIREMENTS: An earned doctorate (DNP, DNE, or PhD). Active, unencumbered Registered Nurse (RN) licensure in the state of primary employment, with eligibility for licensure in additional states as required. Minimum of five (5) years of professional nursing practice experience. Minimum of three (3) years of experience in nursing education, curriculum development, or academic program leadership at the post-secondary level in a programmatically accredited prelicensure nursing program. Experience supervising or providing direction to curriculum or academic program staff preferred. Experience supporting or leading an accreditation self-study or site visit preferred. Experience with online nursing program curriculum design and the instructional design considerations specific to online delivery preferred. Compensation is determined based on the qualifications, experience, and circumstances of each hire. It is uncommon for new employees to start near the top of the salary range. We offer a comprehensive benefits package, including a tuition waiver and reimbursement program, health insurance, paid time off, and a retirement savings plan. The salary range for this position is $127,500 to $172,500. RESPONSIBILITIES: Oversight of Curricular Operations Directly supervise the Associate Director of PN Curriculum, Associate Director of ASN/BSN Curriculum, and Associate Director of MSNDE Curriculum, providing clear direction, performance expectations, and professional development. Set curriculum strategy for each program track and hold Associate Directors accountable for translating that strategy into consistent implementation across all delivery sites and modalities. Establish and maintain structured communication rhythms with Associate Directors to monitor curriculum implementation progress, surface issues, and ensure alignment across program tracks. Conduct regular performance evaluations for direct reports, providing constructive feedback that supports growth and development. Ensure communication aligns with execution of faculty recommendations and evaluation of curriculum performance. Collaboratively develop, review, and update policies and procedures governing curriculum development, review, and implementation across prelicensure nursing programs. Align with the AVP of Instructional Design and Delivery on course development structure, timelines, and quality assurance processes to meet desired outcomes. Align with the AVP of Instructional Design and Delivery on processes and timelines associated with exam proctoring to support successful execution and accountability measures. Collaborate with the Director of Simulation and Lab on the development and placement of simulated learning experiences within the curriculum. Ensure that curriculum policies and procedures align with the university's mission, vision, and operations. Collaborate with the VP of Academic Operations to ensure curriculum requirements are reflected in resource planning including faculty time, facilities, equipment, and technology. Represent Herzing University nursing curriculum with external partners, accrediting bodies, and advisory groups on curriculum-related matters. Oversee work with curriculum advisory committees, including industry experts, alumni, and community representatives, to gather insights and recommendations for curriculum development. Ensure student feedback is incorporated in curriculum development and revision processes through Associate Directors. Develop and maintain relationships with professional organizations and instructional design partners to keep the curriculum responsive to external demands. Design, Development, and Sustainability of Prelicensure Nursing Curriculum Establish the strategic direction for prelicensure nursing curriculum, ensuring alignment with HLC, ACEN, or CCNE accreditation standards, state board of nursing requirements, and current evidence-based nursing practice. Provide leadership to ensure curriculum across all delivery modalities reflects a consistent academic standard and equivalent learning outcomes. Oversee the development and maintenance of curriculum maps, course sequencing frameworks, and program learning outcome structures for all prelicensure nursing programs. Chair with the Nursing Curriculum Committee, which serves as the forum for nursing curriculum decisions across all programs. Collaborate with the Director of Clinical Education, Prelicensure Nursing to ensure clinical curriculum integration aligns with placement capacity, preceptor competency, course learning objectives, and clinical hour requirements. Collaborate with the Director of Lab and Simulation, Prelicensure Nursing to ensure that learning experiences satisfy program and course learning objectives, reinforce concepts introduced in the didactic portion of courses, and prepare students to successfully practice and apply clinical skills in a hands-on setting. Ensure proper curriculum scaffolding amongst courses and modalities of delivery (didactic, lab, clinical) for a cohesive, high-quality student learning experience. Stay current with shifts in regulatory requirements, technologies, and evidence-based practices in nursing education and direct the integration of relevant advances into curriculum design. Oversight of Prelicensure Nursing Curriculum, Assessment, and Continuous Improvement Direct systematic, evidence-based curriculum assessment cycles across all prelicensure nursing programs on a schedule aligned with University Annual Program Review and Comprehensive Program Review cycles and accreditation requirements. Analyze NCLEX pass rate data, NCSBN and Mountain Measure data, program completion data, employer feedback, and graduate outcomes to identify curriculum gaps and direct continuous improvement strategy. Ensure curriculum design supports early identification of and intervention for at-risk students. Oversee collaboration with the Student Learning Data Analyst to review prelicensure nursing performance at the exam, course, and program level and ensure findings are translated into curriculum action. Review semesterly feedback from student and faculty end-of-course surveys and direct recommendations for curriculum improvement to the appropriate Associate Director. Direct and maintain a curriculum change management process that documents all changes, obtains appropriate approvals, and communicates updates to faculty and chairs in a timely and organized manner. Review feedback from clinical partners to ensure that the curriculum prepares students for the realities of clinical practice and meets the needs of the healthcare community. Accreditation and Regulatory Alignment Serve as the subject matter expert on curriculum-related accreditation standards and direct ongoing compliance across all programs. Direct preparation for accreditation self-studies, site visits, and ongoing reporting by ensuring curriculum documentation, evidence, and analysis are maintained and audit-ready, under the guidance of the Academic Compliance team. Maintain current knowledge of state board of nursing rules across all jurisdictions in which Herzing University operates and ensure curriculum meets or exceeds those requirements. Ensure curriculum documentation (syllabi, course guides, competency maps) meets accreditation evidence requirements and is maintained in an organized and audit-ready state. Monitor regulatory and accreditation changes that have curriculum implications and lead proactive curriculum adjustments. Provide regular reporting on curriculum compliance status and accreditation evidence readiness to the Dean of Prelicensure Nursing. Click Here or use the following link to learn more about careers at Herzing University: https://tinyurl.com/HerzingU A pplicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. We do not sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time. Physical Requirements: Must be able to remain in a stationary position 75% of the time. Must be able to occasionally move around the work location. Constantly operates office and/or teach equipment which may include computers, copiers, fax machines, audio/visuals. Frequently uses voice and hearing to communicate with students, staff or colleagues face-to-face or over the telephone. Visually or otherwise identify, observe and assess. Occasionally move, carry, or lift 10 pounds. Must be able to travel up to 15% of time for meetings with stakeholders. Herzing University is committed to providing a diverse environment and is dedicated to fostering a culture and atmosphere of mutual respect. It provides an inclusive and collegial community where individuals are valued, heard and empowered to contribute to the effectiveness of the institution. It is the university’s practice to recruit and hire without discrimination because of skin color, gender, religion, LGBTQi2+ status, disability status, age, national origin, veteran status, or any other status protected by law. https://www.herzing.edu/nondiscrimination-policy Herzing University prohibits sex-based discrimination in any education program or activity that it operates. Individuals may report concerns or questions to the Title IX Coordinator. The notice of nondiscrimination is located at https://www.herzing.edu/title-ix ."
