    "https://recruiting2.ultipro.com/HER1009HRZ/JobBoard/267d2e37-abff-4559-8a18-a754503d3749/OpportunityDetail?opportunityId=4f418691-04db-4eb5-8686-b3ded5894700": {
      "title": "Director of Campus Operations",
      "description": "Director of Campus Operations. Current staff, faculty/adjunct at Herzing University: log into UKG and navigate to Menu > Myself > ​My Company >​ View Opportunities to apply using the internal application process. This role is onsite at Herzing University's Birmingham Campus. Reporting to the Regional Vice President of Operations, with a dotted line to central Academic Operations and Student Affairs, the Director of Campus Operations (DOCO) is responsible for providing leadership to campus academic administrators and faculty who support programs of study, and support staff who provide services at Herzing University. The areas which will be directly supervised by this position include the Program Chairs, Department Chairs, Student Services, Faculty, and administrative staff relevant to these functional areas. The DOCO provides leadership and oversight to campus operations (excluding financial aid and admissions) and ensures compliance and alignment with University, Accreditation, and Regulatory Board standards, policies, and procedures. Additionally, the DOCO is responsible for the development of campus capacity and serves as a primary point of contact for the coordination of facility needs, vendor services, and the promotion of student and employee satisfaction at the campus through collaboration with other campus, regional, and functional leaders. REQUIREMENTS: Master’s degree Two years of educational management experience Three years of Higher Education or Adult Learning experience Preferred: Doctorate degree from a regionally accredited institution Prior leadership experience with pre-licensure professional healthcare programs Five years of professional experience in serving adult-learners Two years of experience in campus operations management Three yeas of experience or more in one of the following areas in Higher Education; teaching, student services, and/or accreditation Compensation is determined based on the qualifications, experience, and circumstances of each hire. It is uncommon for employees to start near the top of the salary range. We offer a comprehensive benefits package, including a tuition waiver and reimbursement program, health insurance, paid time off, and a retirement savings plan. The salary range for this position is $110,500 to $149,500. Responsibilities include (This is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, skills, duties, requirements associated with the job): Serves as the senior leader of campus operations, fostering a positive, inclusive environment aligned with university standards and expectations. Oversees hiring, onboarding, development, and performance management of assigned campus personnel in collaboration with program and university leadership. Manages and monitors campus-level goals related to instructional costs, student retention, and student and employee satisfaction. Represents and promotes the campus through community engagement, strategic partnerships, and external initiatives. Champions a belief in the potential of all students and employees, supporting strong outcomes through proactive leadership and support. Ensures student success and satisfaction by analyzing retention trends, student needs, learning outcomes, program standards, and faculty support and development. Collaborates with campus, programmatic, and functional leaders to execute initiatives; may delegate responsibilities but retains accountability for quality and results. Leads continuous improvement efforts by developing and maintaining campus strategic priorities and analyzing performance data. Ensures alignment with university initiatives by holding staff accountable for local execution and participation in university committees and governance. Supports local initiatives such as Program Advisory Boards and ensures documentation and system expectations are consistently met. There are seven general areas which the Director of Campus Operations must excel in to meet the expectations of the role. Strategic Alignment Promotes and Maintains a Positive Learning Environment and Campus Culture Accurately and Completely Fulfills Administrative Responsibilities Contributes to the Improvement of Curriculum and Instruction Continuous Improvement Communication Development of Campus Capacity Click Here or use the following link to learn more about careers at Herzing University: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DPDCRvjmzHM&t=3s Physical and Other Requirements: Must be able to remain in a stationary position 50% of the time. Ability to move about readily and rapidly, if necessary, around campus, classrooms, clinical settings, etc., to access classrooms, desks, students, office machinery, clinics, patients, etc. Constantly communicates using the spoken word with students, staff and colleagues. Visually or otherwise identify, observe and assess. Operate equipment specific to programmatic track, personal computer, audio-visual equipment, etc. Travel to off-site meetings or conferences or to observe students during clinical education at off-site clinical settings. Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. We do not sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time. Herzing University is committed to providing a diverse environment and is dedicated to fostering a culture and atmosphere of mutual respect. It provides an inclusive and collegial community where individuals are valued, heard and empowered to contribute to the effectiveness of the institution. It is the university’s practice to recruit and hire without discrimination because of skin color, gender, religion, LGBTQi2+ status, disability status, age, national origin, veteran status, or any other status protected by law. https://www.herzing.edu/nondiscrimination-policy Herzing University prohibits sex-based discrimination in any education program or activity that it operates. Individuals may report concerns or questions to the Title IX Coordinator. The notice of nondiscrimination is located at https://www.herzing.edu/title-ix ."
    },
    "https://recruiting2.ultipro.com/HER1009HRZ/JobBoard/267d2e37-abff-4559-8a18-a754503d3749/OpportunityDetail?opportunityId=4b37aba5-caed-434e-8c58-3bb7eeab35d8": {
      "title": "Faculty - Dental Assisting",
      "description": "Faculty - Dental Assisting. Current staff, faculty/adjunct at Herzing University: l og into UKG and navigate to Menu > Myself > ​My Company >​ View Opportunities to apply using the internal application process. Requirements: AAS or diploma in dental assisting from an accredited Dental Assisting program Bachelor's Degree or higher in any field Current MN Dental Assisting license Current CDA (DANB certification) Knowledge of learning principles for adult education, including dental assisting curriculum development, administration, and evaluation. Strong written, verbal and communication skills Compensation is determined based on the qualifications, experience, and circumstances of each hire. It is uncommon for new employees to start near the top of the salary range. We offer a comprehensive benefits package, including a tuition waiver and reimbursement program, health insurance, paid time off, and a retirement savings plan. The salary range for this position is $64,158 to $86,000. Click Here or use the following link to learn more about careers at Herzing University: https://tinyurl.com/HerzingU Faculty duties and responsibilities for this role include: Teaching and learning Scholarship of Teaching and Learning Academic and Institutional Service Within these duties and responsibilities, the following competencies are included. Subject Matter Expertise Effective Communication Pedagogical Mastery Operational Excellence Appreciation and Promotion of Diversity Assessment of Student Learning Utilization of Technology to Enhance Teaching and Learning Continuous Improvement These competencies, as identified by the University's academic community, encompass the knowledge, skills, and behaviors essential to a faculty member's success in the classroom and provide the basis for the faculty hiring, evaluation and development process. Physical Requirements: In addition to teaching in the classroom, developing relationships with our clinical partner sites, and meeting with students during your office hours, our Dental Hygiene program has a clinical component. By applying to this job, you are confirming that you are able to do the following, in both the classroom and at our clinical sites: Consistently communicate using the spoken word with students, staff and colleagues. Visually or otherwise identify, observe and assess. Operate equipment specific to programmatic track, personal computer, audio-visual equipment, clinical equipment, etc. In addition to the above requirements, for programs that include a clinical component, all faculty must be able to: Stand and/or walk for extended periods of time. Ability to reach by extending hands or arms in any direction. Finger dexterity required to manipulate objects. Ability to see and hear within normal parameters. Lift up to 25 pounds. Herzing University is committed to providing a diverse environment and is dedicated to fostering a culture and atmosphere of mutual respect. It provides an inclusive and collegial community where individuals are valued, heard and empowered to contribute to the effectiveness of the institution. Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. We do not sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time. It is the university’s practice to recruit and hire without discrimination because of skin color, gender, religion, LGBTQi2+ status, disability status, age, national origin, veteran status, or any other status protected by law. https://www.herzing.edu/about/diversity Herzing University prohibits sex-based discrimination in any education program or activity that it operates. Individuals may report concerns or questions to the Title IX Coordinator. The notice of nondiscrimination is located at https://www.herzing.edu/title-ix ."
